I think it is very natural that the Longbow should provide their
Rangers with an extra shot, after all it is their quest artifact and
they should get aclimated to it in a snap. It should definitely feel
more comfortable than the Elven bow (for Elven Rangers) and Orcish bow
(for Orcish Rangers).

Also it is not unbalancing because Orcish and Elven Rangers are already
able to fire extra elven or orcish arrows.
It might seem that the disappearing makes the arrows limited. But it
turns out not to be the case after the arrows have been enchanted to +2
and luck has been maximized. After this point only 1 in 200 throws will
result in a lost arrow, which allows one to fire 40000 arrows, enough
for the whole game if starting with a stack of 200 arrows, which is
very normal if the player is careful with his starting elven and orcish
arrows, and carefully kills all elves/orcs (ie not in one move).

Secondly 4 darts with maxed strength (with a gauntlets of power)
provide nearly same damage as 5 arrows. Darts are quite plentiful if
the player is careful to untrap dart traps. You can easily find more
than 1000 in the whole dungeon. This is much more than necessary.
Although you may need to enchant them two times.

So providing an extra multishot with the Longbow should not be
considered unbalancing and should be considered a natural thing,
because the quest artifact should be better than a lowly orcish or
elven bow.

Actually in my current game I have left the Longbow to collect dust in
a box somewhere preferring Elven bow over it. I feel that the Longbow
should be better than my elven bow after all it is supposed to have
more powers. It also provides no other powers except reflection on
which you cannot really depend. I believe giving extra multishot makes
it a very different ability compared to other artifacts and other
powers are not required to make it useful over normal bows.
 
